+    "revolutionism": "The view that the deepest problems of a society cannot be solved inside the existing order, which must be fundamentally changed or overthrown and replaced quickly, by a decisive break such as an uprising, a seizure of power or a mass rupture. It holds that those in power do not give it up willingly and that reforms alone only preserve the old structure.",
