   "Brazilian Integralism": {
     "d": "Advocates an Integral State of corporatism: society organized into corporations of family, municipality and profession under strong, centralized authority. It is grounded in religious traditionalism (God, Fatherland, Family), cultural nationalism and religious authoritarianism, and it rejects civil liberalism, representative democracy, laissez-faire capitalism, state socialism and communism. It defines the nation by culture and spirit and rejects racial nationalism.",
-    "s": "corporatism:1|religious_traditionalism:0.8|religious_authoritarianism:0.6|cultural_nationalism:0.8|centralism:0.5|civil_liberalism:-1|laissez_faire:-0.8|state_socialism:-1|communization:-1|representative_democracy:-0.7|racial_nationalism:-1|organic_democracy:0.5|organic_statism:0.7|protectionism:0.7|thomism:0.5|individualism:-0.43|idealism:0.9|materialism:-0.8|nihilism:-0.8|naturalism:-0.79|dualism:0.61|stoicism:0.5|existentialism:-0.5"
