   "Sansepolcrismo": {
-    "d": "The founding program of the Italian Fascist movement: civic nationalism and imperialist national expansion combined with social-reform demands such as worker representation through corporatism, heavy progressive taxation, land reform and progressivism.",
-    "s": "Progressive_Taxation:0.8|progressivism:0.6|civic_nationalism:0.5|Imperialism:0.5|corporatism:0.4|regressive_taxation:-0.8|productive_democracy:0.4|absolute_idealism:0.3|actual_idealism:0.7|syndicalism:0.89|dirigisme:-0.84|social_market:-0.24|alternative_modernism:0.79|futurism:0.72|individualism:-0.2|pragmatism:0.5|deontology:-0.4|stoicism:0.3|idealism:0.2",
+    "d": "A tax system whose rate increases as the taxable amount rises shifts the burden toward higher incomes, because heavy taxation of great fortunes limits inequality for the working classes (Progressive Taxation). Advances in science, social organization and reform improve the human condition, so that a new Italy breaks with the old order through land reform and worker representation (Progressivism). The nation rests on shared political values and citizenship rather than ethnicity, since every citizen who shares the republic's creed belongs to it (Civic Nationalism). The country should extend its power over other territories as a proletarian nation through force, because expansion answers its claims after the war (Imperialism). A tax in which the rate falls as income rises, through head taxes and payroll caps, is rejected since it burdens workers and spares the rich (against Regressive Taxation).",
