     "d": "Based on the thought of Georges Sorel: syndicalism, in which workers organized in unions and industrial syndicates carry out revolutionary direct action, with the general strike as a social myth and proletarian violence as a class weapon. It scorns parliamentary politics and electoral bargaining, reformist socialism run through the state, bourgeois liberal values and the commerce of unrestrained markets.",
