   "Peronism": {
-    "d": "Argentine doctrine of social justice, economic independence and political sovereignty, the Third Position: dirigisme with a state-led economy, social corporatism that organizes labor within a national movement under a strong leader, civic paternalism with progressive taxation, cultural nationalism and a non-interventionist foreign policy. It rejects laissez-faire liberal capitalism and communization.",
+    "d": "The state steers investment and plans industry with strong directive influence, because economic independence needs a national economy that is led and not left alone (Dirigisme). Labour is organized by sectors within a national movement under state guidance, since social justice requires that workers' syndicates cooperate with employers (Social-Corporatism). Taxes that rise with income shift the burden toward the wealthy, so that the fruits of production are shared with those who create them (Progressive Taxation). The state protects the health, habits and living conditions of citizens through benefits and guidance, because a caring leader secures the dignity of the poor (Civic Paternalism). The country avoids alliances and wars that do not concern its defence, since political sovereignty means choosing its own path (Non-Interventionism). The nation is defined by shared culture, language, traditions and heritage, because its popular identity draws on the country's own history (Cultural Nationalism). A free market without regulation or national direction is rejected since private profit would subordinate the nation to foreign capital (against Laissez-Faire). Class-struggle revolution that abolishes the state and money is rejected, because social harmony between capital and labour is the Third Position (against Communization).",
     "s": "dirigisme:0.8|social_corporatism:0.7|Progressive_Taxation:0.6|civic_paternalism:0.6|Non_Interventionism:0.7|cultural_nationalism:0.6|laissez_faire:-1|communization:-0.8|productive_democracy:0.5|organic_statism:0.5|state_corporatism:0.5|protectionism:0.7|actual_idealism:0.35|individualism:-0.52|pragmatism:0.7|idealism:0.4|naturalism:-0.34|dualism:0.31|utilitarianism:0.3|materialism:-0.3|monism:0.22"
