   "Nihilist Anarchism": {
-    "d": "Combines philosophical nihilism with anarchism. It rejects inherent meaning, objective moral foundations and the assumption that established political or social institutions possess an unquestionable right to authority. It favors individual autonomy and opposition to imposed hierarchies, while leaving room for voluntary association and self-organized forms of cooperation.",
