   "National Radicalism": {
     "d": "A Polish nationalist and authoritarian doctrine associated with the National Radical Camp (ONR), founded in 1934. It envisioned Poland as a Catholic national state, with public and economic life organized according to Catholic principles, hierarchy and corporatist structures. It rejected parliamentary democracy, liberalism and Marxism, advocating a strong state and the subordination of individual political interests to the national community. Its nationalism was ethnically exclusionary and explicitly antisemitic, promoting the marginalization and exclusion of Jews from national life. The movement emphasized Catholic traditionalism, national solidarity, social discipline and centralized political authority. The original ONR split in 1934 into ONR-ABC and ONR-Falanga, whose later programmes developed in different directions.",
